    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Rebecca Sutton Koeser",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "A utility to update all checksums makes me a bit nervous; it seems that any utility like that would need a way to be very selective (lists of pids, datastreams, etc.).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Would it be possible to add a \"re-migrate\" sort of option to the inline-to-managed migration script? That is, I would like to be able to run it on XML content that has already been migrated, but with the corrected options-- so that the stored xml will be formatted correctly (whatever that means) for the existing checksum to be accurate again.  I think that would make it possible to clean up the invalid checksums caused by the migration in a very targeted fashion, and would make me a lot more confident in repository content validity than just calculating new checksums wholesale.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "I see you have this targeted for Fedora 3.6; is it possible that the clean-up solution (whatever it is) could be back-ported to maintenance releases of other versions of Fedora?  In particular, it would be really great to be able to clean up all the invalid xml checksums and do a full checksum audit before upgrading to a new version of Fedora, for comparison after.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
