  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Talked about on Feb 9th call. Clearly there's a need to fix the bug that caused this. Also, a utility to get people out of this situation is needed. Would a separate \"freshen your checksums\" utility or option in the rebuilder to correct checksums (with a big warning about \"this is changing your low-level-stored xml\") be good?</p>",
     "created": "09/Feb/12 5:31 PM",
     "id": "12237",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11021/comment/12237",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "09/Feb/12 5:31 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Rebecca Sutton Koeser",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>A utility to update all checksums makes me a bit nervous; it seems that any utility like that would need a way to be very selective (lists of pids, datastreams, etc.).</p>\n\n<p>Would it be possible to add a \"re-migrate\" sort of option to the inline-to-managed migration script? That is, I would like to be able to run it on XML content that has already been migrated, but with the corrected options-- so that the stored xml will be formatted correctly (whatever that means) for the existing checksum to be accurate again.  I think that would make it possible to clean up the invalid checksums caused by the migration in a very targeted fashion, and would make me a lot more confident in repository content validity than just calculating new checksums wholesale.</p>\n\n<p>I see you have this targeted for Fedora 3.6; is it possible that the clean-up solution (whatever it is) could be back-ported to maintenance releases of other versions of Fedora?  In particular, it would be really great to be able to clean up all the invalid xml checksums and do a full checksum audit before upgrading to a new version of Fedora, for comparison after.</p>",
     "created": "10/Feb/12 6:43 PM",
     "id": "12238",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11021/comment/12238",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Rebecca Sutton Koeser",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "10/Feb/12 6:43 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Rebecca Sutton Koeser",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I've been thinking about this problem some more, and wondered if it would make more sense to create a stand-alone script (something that could be made available independent of a full-blown release of Fedora) that could selectively clean up or canonicalize the xml to make it match existing checksums.  Obviously, something like this would need a lot of testing and checks, since it will have to bypass the Fedora APIs (entirely? partially?).  </p>\n\n<p>Since fixing this is a current need for our production repository, it's possible I or someone on my team could write a python script to do this repository clean-up, if we knew what exactly should be done (whether and how to reformat/re-canonicalize the xml, or update the checksums), along with any other recommendations from the Fedora developers (approach, safeguards, etc).</p>",
     "created": "24/Feb/12 9:20 PM",
     "id": "12253",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11021/comment/12253",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4e8b233c8006ba9915a",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/a27b189f53110c93b66a08557fa79dee?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRK-0.png",
